                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7278502a-af8b-454b-b596-99a6cb624c2b</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">SHELF BRACKET / 250 mm / FOUR ALTERNATIVE LOAD CASES
Units mm, N. X projects from wall; Y is width; Z is UP. Payload is kg per bracket.
1 BASELINE &gt; 2 OPTIMIZATION &gt; 3 VOXEL VERIFICATION &gt; 4 EXTRACT &gt; 5 FINAL FEM.
Case 1 distributed; 2 front; 3 front-right; 4 front-left. Every case adds shelf share and bracket self-weight.
Two wall holes and two shelf holes, with reserved tool access. EXTRACT restores nominal CAD plates and holes independently of the voxel grid.
Default: 5 mm cells, CPU AMG (2). CUDA (4) requires a separately configured GPU runtime. Never change solver while a job is running.
ABS is an injection-molding reference, not printed-material qualification. Wall pads are rigid idealizations.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
